Declare it with `function*` and `yield` the counter inside an ordinary `for` loop. Each `yield` pauses the function until the next value is requested.

```js
const range = function* (end) {
  for (let i = 0; i < end; i++) yield i;
};

for (const i of range(5)) console.log(i);
// Logs: 0, 1, 2, 3, 4
[...range(3)]; // [0, 1, 2]
```

Values are produced lazily: nothing runs until the caller asks for a value, so `range(1e9)` costs nothing until you iterate it. Calling `range(5)` returns a generator object, not an array.

