Typing `import` for every module each time you open the REPL gets tedious as the project grows. An autoloader reads the models folder, dynamically imports each file, and puts its export into the REPL's global context.

```js
// console.js (run with: node console.js)
import repl from 'node:repl';
import { readdir } from 'node:fs/promises';

const server = repl.start('> ');
for (const file of await readdir('./src/models')) {
  const { default: model } = await import(`./src/models/${file}`);
  server.context[model.name] = model; // Post, Author, ...
}
// > Post.find(1)
```

