`pluck(attr)` returns the values of one attribute, one per record. `select(...attrs)` returns partial records: new objects containing only the chosen keys. Both are thin wrappers around `map()`.

```js
class RecordSet extends Array {
  pluck(attribute) {
    return RecordSet.from(super.map(record => record[attribute]));
  }

  select(...attributes) {
    return RecordSet.from(super.map(record =>
      Object.fromEntries(attributes.map(a => [a, record[a]]))
    ));
  }
}

