Check whether the URL has an extension. If it doesn't, try `url + '.html'` first and fall back to `url/index.html`. The root URL `/` is a special case that maps to `index.html`.

```js
import { existsSync } from 'node:fs';
import { join, extname } from 'node:path';

const root = join(import.meta.dirname, 'public');

function resolveFileName(requestUrl) {
  if (requestUrl === '/') return 'index.html';
  if (extname(requestUrl)) return requestUrl;          // '/app.js'
  if (existsSync(join(root, requestUrl + '.html')))
    return requestUrl + '.html';                        // '/about' -> '/about.html'
  return join(requestUrl, 'index.html');                // '/docs' -> '/docs/index.html'
}
```

Two files can match the same URL, so you must pick a priority; here `about.html` wins. `existsSync` blocks the event loop briefly. That is fine for a small tool, but a busy server would use the async `fs/promises` API.

