Make every builder return plain pattern text, so any result can be passed into another builder. Define `hex` once, then `repeat(hex, 3)` and `repeat(hex, 6)` build short and long CSS color codes from the same piece.

```js
const digit = String.raw`\d`;
const range = (start, end) => `[${start}-${end}]`;
const or = (...patterns) => `(?:${patterns.join('|')})`;
const repeat = (pattern, times) => `(?:${pattern}){${times}}`;

const hex = or(digit, range('a', 'f'));  // defined once
const shortColor = new RegExp(`^#${repeat(hex, 3)}$`);
const longColor = new RegExp(`^#${repeat(hex, 6)}$`);

shortColor.test('#a1b');   // true
longColor.test('#a1b2c3'); // true
longColor.test('#a1b2cz'); // false
```

Pieces only compose safely if each is self-contained: wrap alternations and multi-character pieces in `(?:...)` so a neighboring quantifier or `|` can't change their meaning.

