Names are case-sensitive (`getUser` and `getuser` are different functions). Common prefixes: `get`/`fetch` (read), `create`/`update`/`delete` (write), `to`/`format` (convert), and `handle` or `on` for event handlers. Class methods follow the same rules.

Use **`UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`** for fixed, hard-coded values known before the program runs, usually at the top of a module: configuration and "magic numbers" such as `MAX_RETRIES` or `API_BASE_URL`. Use **`camelCase`** for a `const` whose value is computed at runtime, even though it is never reassigned.

```js
const MAX_UPLOAD_MB = 10;
