Scale S and L to 0–1, compute the chroma factor `a = S × min(L, 1 − L)`, then for each channel subtract a clamped amount from L and multiply by 255 (the standard HSL→RGB formula). **Round** the fractional results before using them.

```js
// h: 0-360, s and l: 0-100 → [r, g, b] in 0-255
const hslToRgb = (h, s, l) => {
  s /= 100;
  l /= 100;
  const k = n => (n + h / 30) % 12;
  const a = s * Math.min(l, 1 - l);
  const f = n =>
    l - a * Math.max(-1, Math.min(k(n) - 3, Math.min(9 - k(n), 1)));
  return [255 * f(0), 255 * f(8), 255 * f(4)];
};

hslToRgb(13, 100, 11); // [56.1, 12.155000000000006, 0]
hslToRgb(13, 100, 11).map(Math.round); // [56, 12, 0]
```

