`perspective()` sets how far the viewer is from the element. Without it, `rotateY()` just looks like horizontal squashing with no depth; smaller values give stronger depth. The hover rule must repeat it because a new `transform` value replaces the whole function list. Leave `perspective()` out and the hover state renders flat, with no depth.

