.perspective-card {
  transform: perspective(1500px) rotateY(15deg);
  transition: transform 1s ease;
}

.perspective-card:hover {
  transform: perspective(3000px) rotateY(5deg);
}
```

When both lists have the same functions in the same order, the browser interpolates them function by function; otherwise it falls back to matrix interpolation, which can take an odd path. The `perspective` property (on a parent) is the alternative when several children should share one 3D viewpoint.

