Physical. Even though it is defined in the CSS Logical Properties spec, `inset` always sets `top`, `right`, `bottom`, and `left`, regardless of `direction` or writing mode. For layouts that should mirror in right-to-left languages (Arabic, Hebrew), use the logical properties `inset-inline-start/end`, `inset-block-start/end`, or the shorthands `inset-inline` and `inset-block`.

```css
/* Always the physical right edge */
.close { position: absolute; top: 0; right: 0; }

/* The "end" edge: right in LTR, left in RTL */
.close { position: absolute; inset-block-start: 0; inset-inline-end: 0; }
```

In horizontal writing modes, block = vertical (top/bottom) and inline = the text direction (left/right).

