A modern reset fixes a few annoying defaults instead of erasing all browser styles: border-box sizing everywhere, no default `body` margin, media that doesn't overflow its container, form controls that inherit the page font, long words that wrap instead of overflowing, and reduced motion when the user asks for it.

```css
*, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }

body { margin: 0; line-height: 1.5; }

img, picture, svg, video { display: block; max-width: 100%; }

input, button, textarea, select { font: inherit; }

p, h1, h2, h3 { overflow-wrap: break-word; }

sub, sup { line-height: 0; }   /* don't stretch the line's height */

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  *, *::before, *::after { animation-duration: 0.01ms !important; transition-duration: 0.01ms !important; }
}
```

