It is set on the children of a snap container and defines which part of each child lines up with the container's snapport (the visible area) when scrolling settles. `start` aligns the child's leading edge with the container's start edge, `center` centers the child in view, `end` aligns the trailing edges, and `none` (default) makes the child not a snap target.

```css
.carousel { overflow-x: auto; scroll-snap-type: x mandatory; }

.carousel > .slide {
  scroll-snap-align: center;   /* each slide settles centered */
}
```

`start` suits full-width slides and lists; `center` suits "peek" carousels where neighbors are partly visible. `scroll-padding` on the container offsets the snap position (e.g. for a sticky header).

