Call the dispatch of a `useReducer` whose reducer always returns a new value, e.g. `useReducer(x => x + 1, 0)`; each dispatch changes state, so React re-renders. Needing this usually means the UI depends on data React doesn't know about (a mutated object, a global variable, a browser API), and the real fix is to put that data in state or subscribe to it properly.

