Three problems: an early `return` before a hook breaks the **Rules of Hooks** (hooks must run in the same order every render); `addListener` is deprecated in favor of `addEventListener('change', ...)`; and `[]` means a new `query` is ignored. `useSyncExternalStore` fixes all three and handles server rendering.

```jsx
function useMediaQuery(query) {
  const subscribe = useCallback(notify => {
    const mql = window.matchMedia(query);
    mql.addEventListener('change', notify);
    return () => mql.removeEventListener('change', notify);
  }, [query]);

  return useSyncExternalStore(
    subscribe,
    () => window.matchMedia(query).matches,
    () => false                               // server render
  );
}

// const isNarrow = useMediaQuery('(max-width: 400px)');
// const prefersDark = useMediaQuery('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)');
```

`useCallback` keeps `subscribe` stable so React only resubscribes when `query` changes. For pure styling, a CSS `@media` rule is still simpler.

