In React 18 and earlier, calling `useLayoutEffect` during server rendering printed a warning, because layout effects can't run on the server. Aliasing to `useEffect` when there's no `window` silenced it. Neither effect runs on the server anyway, so behavior was the same. React 19 no longer prints that warning, so you can usually call `useLayoutEffect` directly.

```jsx
// Legacy helper, still common in libraries
const useIsomorphicLayoutEffect =
  typeof window !== 'undefined' ? useLayoutEffect : useEffect;

function Tooltip({ anchorRef }) {
  const ref = useRef(null);
  useIsomorphicLayoutEffect(() => {
    // measure anchorRef.current and position ref.current before paint
  }, []);
  return <div ref={ref} role="tooltip" />;
}
```

Remember what `useLayoutEffect` is for: measuring or adjusting the DOM before the browser paints. With server rendering, content that depends on that measurement still appears only after hydration.

